{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sdv7V39BMpoDVkuhGRD666","type":"tool_result","content":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/aa4be1bfea8619b294a9da9acaf7f857db8735b4d1aab9b216520381c24c5c21.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task catalog-handoff: Prepare the fleet catalog patch for the morning operator. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"handoff\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:e7ebc582ee607de986092dc37f77b9d1aa9ddee5b8bb214f5016f1ddc6f8df51\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"git apply --stat handoff/catalog-row.patch >/dev/null && test -s handoff/README.md\"],\"description\":\"The patch parses as a git patch and the handoff note exists.\",\"id\":\"catalog-patch-wellformed\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"handoff\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"The morning catalog declaration is one git apply plus one review, not authoring work\",\"The operator knows the patch is what stops the sync service from pruning the staged weights again\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Write handoff/catalog-row.patch per spec claim 5.2 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5): a git format patch against the fleet configuration repository adding the workload checkpoint as a snapshot-layout artifact row assigned to both hosts, following the existing snapshot-layout precedent row in that repository's model library file, with pinned upstream revision and per-file byte counts read from the staged copy under /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8 (or from the library mount when staging has not finished). Add handoff/README.md explaining exactly what the operator applies and verifies in the morning — and state the urgency plainly: the fleet's local-models sync retires any staged artifact that has no catalog row (it pruned the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes on 2026-08-29, triggered at boot, on rebuilds, and on model-sync service starts, which is why tonight's campaign had to re-stage 185.6 GB per node); applying this patch is what ends that hazard permanently, and it must be applied BEFORE any rebuild or any restart of the model-sync trigger service. The patch is prepared, never applied, by this campaign. Boundaries: touch only handoff/.\",\"id\":\"catalog-handoff\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:7f3033dbd7a5c6b695b70874814d89053eec1372194895793dc8534f9f4d03ed\",\"title\":\"Prepare the fleet catalog patch for the morning operator\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"bfd358b923b35a4a80dad2163d7e8ec16aaf81b6\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-5e8a586bb7ac/catalog-handoff\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"handoff\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/catalog-handoff-7f3033dbd7a5c6b6\",\"taskId\":\"catalog-handoff\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/5e8a586bb7ac/catalog-handoff\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":0,\"recheckedCursor\":0,\"registrationId\":\"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"959dbb14-0dd9-4eec-837f-bf0ff1384901","uuid":"6baf7667-847f-46ec-84c5-bb04bd87a5c6","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:35:39.364Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/aa4be1bfea8619b294a9da9acaf7f857db8735b4d1aab9b216520381c24c5c21.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task catalog-handoff: Prepare the fleet catalog patch for the morning operator. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"handoff\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:e7ebc582ee607de986092dc37f77b9d1aa9ddee5b8bb214f5016f1ddc6f8df51\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"git apply --stat handoff/catalog-row.patch >/dev/null && test -s handoff/README.md\"],\"description\":\"The patch parses as a git patch and the handoff note exists.\",\"id\":\"catalog-patch-wellformed\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"handoff\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"The morning catalog declaration is one git apply plus one review, not authoring work\",\"The operator knows the patch is what stops the sync service from pruning the staged weights again\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Write handoff/catalog-row.patch per spec claim 5.2 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5): a git format patch against the fleet configuration repository adding the workload checkpoint as a snapshot-layout artifact row assigned to both hosts, following the existing snapshot-layout precedent row in that repository's model library file, with pinned upstream revision and per-file byte counts read from the staged copy under /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8 (or from the library mount when staging has not finished). Add handoff/README.md explaining exactly what the operator applies and verifies in the morning — and state the urgency plainly: the fleet's local-models sync retires any staged artifact that has no catalog row (it pruned the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes on 2026-08-29, triggered at boot, on rebuilds, and on model-sync service starts, which is why tonight's campaign had to re-stage 185.6 GB per node); applying this patch is what ends that hazard permanently, and it must be applied BEFORE any rebuild or any restart of the model-sync trigger service. The patch is prepared, never applied, by this campaign. Boundaries: touch only handoff/.\",\"id\":\"catalog-handoff\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:7f3033dbd7a5c6b695b70874814d89053eec1372194895793dc8534f9f4d03ed\",\"title\":\"Prepare the fleet catalog patch for the morning operator\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"bfd358b923b35a4a80dad2163d7e8ec16aaf81b6\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-5e8a586bb7ac/catalog-handoff\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"handoff\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/catalog-handoff-7f3033dbd7a5c6b6\",\"taskId\":\"catalog-handoff\",\"