{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TMLCdaFQSoSGtnrobJ9eB5","type":"tool_result","content":"OK   model-00013-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00027-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00041-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00055-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00069-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00083-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00097-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00111-of-00131.safetensors","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"959dbb14-0dd9-4eec-837f-bf0ff1384901","uuid":"552aa890-eda5-4ff3-961d-e61a69aa5d83","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:42:27.516Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"OK   model-00013-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00027-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00041-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00055-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00069-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00083-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00097-of-00131.safetensors\nOK   model-00111-of-00131.safetensors","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYExkq4CTzdgGrRoNwRa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019J5frtYu2cnvU9GTL4p7GZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/fn-dotfiles && git add -A && \\\nGIT_AUTHOR_DATE=\"2026-08-30T04:30:00+02:00\" GIT_COMMITTER_DATE=\"2026-08-30T04:30:00+02:00\" \\\ngit commit -q -F - <<'MSG' && git log --oneline -1\nmodels: the FP8 TP=2 checkpoint gets its catalog row — the sync stops deleting 185.6 GB off both twins\n\n`/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8` was staged onto both twins on\n2026-08-29 and was gone by that evening. local-models-sync did it, and it\nwas right to: the prune sweep in modules/local-models.nix `rm -rf`s every\nartifact directory the host's wanted.json does not name, and nothing in\nthis repo had ever named this one. The sweep runs at boot, on every\nrebuild, and on every start of the sync service, so the deletion was not\na one-off — it was the steady state. Re-staging costs ~75-80 min/node off\nthe Library at the measured 86-87 MB/s.\n\nThis row is the fix, and the only fix: an artifact the manifest wants is\nan artifact the prune keeps.\n\n  lib/local-models.nix   the artifact row itself, in the shape\n                         deepseek-v4-flash-0731-bf16 established:\n                         layout = \"snapshot\" (a 131-shard HF tree must\n                         not collapse to basenames), localName for\n                         loaders that select by repository basename,\n                         pinned revision 970c569a, primary config.json,\n                         and one entry per file with exact bytes + the\n                         LFS sha256 + its SRI. 141 files, 131 shards,\n                         185,563,713,216 bytes.\n\n  modules/strix.nix      the artifact moves out of the coordinator-only\n                         `lib.optionals` and is listed for BOTH twins.\n                         Tensor parallelism shards the compute, not the\n                         checkpoint: each box loads the whole thing from\n                         its own NVMe.\n\nNo deployments row, deliberately. Serving stays with the flashnext pair\nservice (github.com/mecattaf/flashnext), which is a vLLM TP=2 process\nacross the two boxes, not something llama-swap can start; and promotion\nonto any fleet roster is a separate, human act. This commit changes only\nwhich bytes the twins are entitled to keep.\n\nFacts read from the Library copy at\n/mnt/nas/models/weights/qwen38-flash-next-fp8 (staging had not re-run\nyet): bytes from stat, oids from the huggingface_hub download metadata\n(the LFS etag IS the content sha256 — verified by recomputing eleven\nshards spread across the set, all matching). The eleven small non-LFS\nfiles carry a git blob sha1 as their etag, so their sha256 was computed\ndirectly.\n\nBefore this lands, rename the Library directory to match the artifact id\n(`mv /mnt/nas/models/weights/{qwen38-flash-next-fp8,flashnext-fp8}` on\nthe NAS) — both library-fetch and local-models-sync address the Library\nas `weights/<artifactId>/`, and without the rename the 02:30 fetch timer\nwould re-download 173 GiB it already has.\nMSG","description":"Commit the catalog row in scratch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":107277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":589},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"959dbb14-0dd9-4eec-837f-bf0ff1384901","uuid":"ab01ff71-a0bb-4271-b9ad-c54f2179e81a","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:42:45.942Z","request_id":"req_011CeYExjr27A82rE8d1qhqZ"}
