{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RJ8xfe3EKvAC7Pb1UnsxbD","type":"tool_result","content":"  959 51740 /tmp/catalog-row.patch\nFrom b8f093edbdf9eca7503a3b1c91b90fea907c0e2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Tom Leger <thomas@leger.run>\nDate: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 04:30:00 +0200\nSubject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?models:=20the=20FP8=20TP=3D2=20checkpoint=20get?=\n =?UTF-8?q?s=20its=20catalog=20row=20=E2=80=94=20the=20sync=20stops=20dele?=\n =?UTF-8?q?ting=20185.6=20GB=20off=20both=20twins?=\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n\n`/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8` was staged onto both twins on\n2026-08-29 and was gone by that evening. local-models-sync did it, and it\nwas right to: the prune sweep in modules/local-models.nix `rm -rf`s every\nartifact directory the host's wanted.json does not name, and nothing in\nthis repo had ever named this one. The sweep runs at boot, on every\nrebuild, and on every start of the sync service, so the deletion was not\na one-off — it was the steady state. Re-staging costs ~75-80 min/node off\nthe Library at the measured 86-87 MB/s.\n\nThis row is the fix, and the only fix: an artifact the manifest wants is\n...TAIL...\n+      ]\n+      ++ lib.optionals (config.networking.hostName == \"coordinator\") [\n         # Priority Mage family: the unified VLM and the low-latency generation\n         # and editing variants. Base and RL checkpoints are intentionally\n         # omitted; their quality gain does not justify 5-7.5x more steps here.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/5e8a586bb7ac/catalog-handoff","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"959dbb14-0dd9-4eec-837f-bf0ff1384901","uuid":"bdc0097e-f02b-40c2-bcbc-757606072f9e","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:43:03.587Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  959 51740 /tmp/catalog-row.patch\nFrom b8f093edbdf9eca7503a3b1c91b90fea907c0e2a Mon Sep 17 00: