{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYFA1sVFZ5g4eZ1fzHZ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0128tMWAva46UuwMzen35dmV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add handoff/catalog-row.patch handoff/README.md && git status --porcelain && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG' && git log --oneline -1 && git status --porcelain && echo \"CLEAN\"\ncatalog-handoff: the morning catalog patch, and why it must land before any rebuild\n\n`handoff/catalog-row.patch` is a git format-patch against mecattaf/dotfiles\n`99d72cf5`, prepared and never applied (ruling P13, claim 7.3). It adds\n`flashnext-fp8` to `lib/local-models.nix` as a snapshot-layout artifact —\nthe shape `deepseek-v4-flash-0731-bf16` established — with the pinned\nupstream revision `970c569a`, `primary = \"config.json\"`, and 141 file\nentries carrying exact bytes, content sha256, and SRI; 131 shards,\n185,563,713,216 bytes. `modules/strix.nix` moves the artifacts list out of\nits coordinator-only `lib.optionals` so both twins declare it: tensor\nparallelism shards the compute, not the checkpoint.\n\nFacts read from the Library copy, since node staging had not re-run —\nbytes from stat, oids from the huggingface_hub download metadata, whose\nLFS etag is the content sha256 (recomputed on eleven shards spread across\nthe set, all matching); the eleven small non-LFS files hashed directly.\nVerified out of tree: the patch `git am`s clean onto a pristine clone, the\ncatalog evaluates, `materializeArtifact` yields\n`/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8` with 141 files, and nixfmt is clean\non both touched files.\n\nNo deployments row: serving stays with the pair service, and promotion is\na separate human act.\n\n`handoff/README.md` is the operator's page. It states the urgency without\nsoftening it — local-models-sync `rm -rf`s any artifact directory\nwanted.json does not name, at boot, on every rebuild, and on every start\nof the service; that is what deleted the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes\non 2026-08-29 and cost tonight a 185.6 GB per-node re-stage. This row is\nthe only thing that ends it, and it must be in the deployed configuration\nBEFORE any rebuild or any restart of the sync service. The note also\ncarries the one prerequisite the patch cannot express: the Library\ndirectory on the NAS must be renamed to the artifact id first, or the\n02:30 fetch timer re-downloads 173 GiB it already has.\nMSG","description":"Commit the handoff deliverables"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":120776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"959dbb14-0dd9-4eec-837f-bf0ff1384901","uuid":"7f997f32-39ac-45ba-8d84-9da48908cfb0","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:45:14.447Z","request_id":"req_011CeYF9zsxfkgcrHfR5iEoi"}
