{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYFBasswF2XdcD9ANf8g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Committed `513ae39` on `tally-work/flashnext-5e8a586bb7ac/catalog-handoff`; `git status --porcelain` is empty. Both files are inside the `handoff/` write boundary.\n\n**`handoff/catalog-row.patch`** — a `git format-patch` against mecattaf/dotfiles `99d72cf5`, prepared and never applied:\n\n- `lib/local-models.nix`: `flashnext-fp8` artifact row, inserted right after the `deepseek-v4-flash-0731-bf16` precedent and built in its shape — `layout = \"snapshot\"`, `localName = \"Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8\"`, pinned `revision = 970c569adaca6b35532111fd6b27351b2baefe50`, `primary = \"config.json\"`, 141 file entries with exact `bytes` + `oid` + SRI `hash`. 131 shards, 185,563,713,216 bytes.\n- `modules/strix.nix`: `services.local-models.artifacts` moves out of the coordinator-only `lib.optionals`, so both twins declare it.\n- No `deployments` row — serving stays with the pair service, and promotion is a separate human act (P13).\n\nData provenance: node staging had not re-run (`/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8` is absent), so bytes/oids came from the Library copy. `bytes` from `stat`; `oid` from the `huggingface_hub` download metadata, whose LFS etag is the content sha256 — verified by recomputing `sha256sum` on eleven shards spread across the set (00001…00130), all matching; the eleven small non-LFS files (git-blob-sha1 etags) were hashed directly.\n\nVerified out of tree: the patch `git am`s clean onto a pristine clone, the catalog evaluates, `materializeArtifact` yields `/var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8` with 141 files, the four applicable catalog assertions hold, and `nixfmt --check` is clean on both files. Acceptance criterion `catalog-patch-wellformed` passes.\n\n**`handoff/README.md`** — the operator page: the prune mechanism quoted from `modules/local-models.nix`, the 2026-08-29 deletion from both nodes and its 185.6 GB/node cost, the stated ordering (this row must be in the deployed config *before* any rebuild or any `local-models-sync` restart), a three-point review list, eval/deploy/verify commands, and the closing proof — `systemctl restart local-models-sync` and the 131 shards survive.\n\nTwo things worth your attention:\n\n1. **The patch has a prerequisite it cannot express.** Both `library-fetch` and `local-models-sync` address the Library as `weights/<artifactId>/`, but the NAS directory is named `qwen38-flash-next-fp8` while the artifact id must be `flashnext-fp8` (that is the node path every campaign script uses). Step 0 of the note is a `mv` on the NAS; without it the 02:30 fetch timer re-downloads 173 GiB it already has.\n2. **The first sync after the patch deletes stray files from the node copies** — `README.md`, `LICENSE`, `.gitattributes`, `.cache/huggingface/`, and `MANIFEST.sha256` (what `scripts/stage-weights.sh` writes). Excluding those files matches the precedent row and none are load-bearing, but the `MANIFEST.sha256` interaction is permanent, so the note calls it out as steady state rather than a fault."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":414,"cache_read_input_tokens":122091,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":414},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"959dbb14-0dd9-4eec-837f-bf0ff1384901","uuid":"eb695a65-ec8b-40ac-8a80-fc1462f034bf","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:45:37.484Z","request_id":"req_011CeYFBZotSPUCcmMe6Y7WT"}
